            <ArticleTitle>One-year follow-up of recanalization of totally occluded aortocoronary saphenous vein grafts using transluminal extraction atherectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>636-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recanalization of totally occluded aortocoronary saphenous vein grafts with extraction atherectomy was successful in 80% of patients. Whereas all patients with unsuccessful procedures were dead at 1 year, 75% of those with successful procedures are alive and free of events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
